-- statement:
--   Exact primorial certificate for the primes up to $1499$:
--   $$\prod_{p \le 1499,\; p \text{ prime}} p = N \quad\text{and}\quad \prod_{p \le 1499,\; p \text{ prime}} (p-1) = D,$$
--   with $N$ and $D$ the two explicit integers stated in the formal statement (a $636$-digit primorial and its shifted product). This is a pure finite data certificate: it anchors the Rosser–Schoenfeld product-bound legs above $1500$ the same way primorial_certificate_1049 anchors the $1050\dots1500$ leg, so that each range leg only has to telescope the Euler product over its own primes instead of re-verifying the primorial from scratch.
-- source:
--   Pure finite computation certificate (companion to TaoFivePrimes.primorial_certificate_691 and TaoFivePrimes.primorial_certificate_1049): the exact values of the primorial $\prod_{p\le 1499} p$ and of $\prod_{p\le 1499}(p-1)$, to serve as the verified anchor for the range legs of Rosser–Schoenfeld Theorem 23 (4.10) above $1500$.

import Mathlib.NumberTheory.PrimeCounting

namespace TaoFivePrimes
theorem primorial_certificate_1499 :
    ∏ p ∈ Nat.primesLE 1499, (p : ℕ) =  ∧
    ∏ p ∈ Nat.primesLE 1499, ((p : ℕ) - 1) =  := by sorry
end TaoFivePrimes
